WEBVTT

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:07.690
Oojima
Yuuki
Election
Headquarters<b>
Starting today, the club room is our campaign headquarters,</b>

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:10.420
and I will be acting as campaign president.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:12.200
We're finally getting things in order.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.240
Non-chan is very excited!

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:16.780
We have to make flags for our speeches.

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:17.990
Let's make posters first.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.160
I'd be more than happy to be the announcer.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:23.200
I can't help out directly since I'm a teacher,

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.120
but I can at least lend you some advice.

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:27.600
Vote... for...

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:28.500
Guys!

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:31.260
My candidacy form has been filed!

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:36.020
Well, then let's get into campaign mode!

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:37.200
Right!

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:37.890
Yeah.

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:42.270
Well? What should I do next?

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:47.360
Um... What <i>should</i> he do next?

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:23.740
As part of Takafuji Academy's presidential election process,

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:26.120
the school will hold a primary prior to the actual election.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:29.210
If we don't pass the primaries, we can't run.

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:30.720
Primaries, huh?

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:33.460
That's where all of the bubbly candidates pop.

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:35.240
Bubbly candidates?

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:37.240
They're the weak candidates.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:40.280
They have neither popularity nor budget, and their policies are inadequate.

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:43.340
Even if they ran, they'd pop like bubbles.

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:44.470
That sounds just like Ooshima!

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:47.850
That's why we're here thinking of ways to prevent that.

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:51.980
You need at least 10 percent of the vote to pass the primaries.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:54.980
That's 10 percent of 6,000 students,

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:57.700
so we need 600 votes.

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:00.220
How are we supposed to get 600 votes?

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:01.540
By...

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:04.020
making a good manifesto, I guess.

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:06.740
We need something that can easily attract anyone.

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:09.790
In that case, how about increasing the club budgets?

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:11.920
Let's double the Food Research Club's budget.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:17.000
Non-chan thinks a snack allowance would make everyone happy!

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.050
An alcohol allowance would be nice.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:24.120
Cash allowances might lead to corruption,

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:26.120
so how about making snacks free?

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:28.060
Free Yaoi Sticks.

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:30.360
All of those are just distributing favors.

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:34.480
I'd never win with a manifesto like that.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:38.690
The problem is that we don't have any know-how on campaigning.

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:41.960
It'd be really helpful if we had someone with experience.

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:44.720
We don't know anyone like that.

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:48.870
Excuse me.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:52.540
Wow! Yakkun, long time no see!

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:53.480
Isn't he...

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:54.710
...President Mouri?

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:57.000
It's been a while, Non-chan.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.090
You've grown.

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:01.320
Of course. Non-chan is a senior.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:03.340
It's only natural that I'd grow.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:07.100
I've grown to exude the charms of a woman.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:11.310
Great. If that's the case, your future should be very interesting.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:12.890
Obviously!

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:16.700
Are you friends with the president, too, Non-chan-senpai?

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:20.980
Yes. Yakkun was in my class during our freshman year.

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:25.300
Wait. You're friends with the president, too, Yuuki?

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:26.620
Yeah... I guess.

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:28.520
You're running in the election, yes?

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:30.400
Huh? Y-Yeah.

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.800
Thanks to you, I guess.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:36.180
Actually, my visit today is regarding that.

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:36.750
Huh?

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:39.520
Let me be frank.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:43.380
Would you allow us, the Public Safety Commission, to assist Oojima-kun in his campaign?

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:44.130
What?

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:46.740
A-Are you serious?

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:47.510
I am.

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:49.180
But why me?

00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:51.880
If you're after his body, you're too late.

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:53.740
Yuuki-senpai's body,

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:57.650
from the top of his head to the tips of his toes, already belongs to me.

00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:59.400
Would you be willing to share him with me?

00:04:59.400 --> 00:04:59.940
Yume!

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:00.880
Right.

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:07.440
They wouldn't offer to help unless there were something in it for them.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:08.950
That's correct.

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:13.200
Our offer to help stems from a selfish reason.

00:05:13.510 --> 00:05:15.220
A selfish reason?

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:15.830
Yes.

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:17.640
The Public Safety Commission

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:20.840
does not wish to relinquish the position to either Finance or General Affairs.

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:24.720
Why don't you wish to relinquish the position?

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:28.340
Even if you guys can't run this year, you should be able to try again next year.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:31.780
An election is typically won by the party in power.

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:35.850
Once the regime is handed over, it is difficult to get it back.

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:39.380
So, if an independent like Yuuki is elected president,

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:43.140
everyone will be on the same level for next year.

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:43.940
Precisely.

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:45.660
But why choose me?

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:47.360
There are plenty of other candidates.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:52.620
That's because you have the
potential to pass the primary election.

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:54.700
I do?

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:55.750
Yes.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:59.880
The other day, Shinonome's manifesto was disclosed,

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:04.040
and according to our research, her
approval rating dropped by 10 percent.

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:05.260
10 percent?

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:06.510
How did that happen?

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:11.980
There are minor reasons, like putting too much emphasis on financial-aid policy reform,

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:14.140
but mainly, there are many who oppose the club reforms.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:18.500
The students in clubs that would receive budget cuts are against her now.

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:22.680
Basically, if we show we're against the club reforms,

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:24.780
we can get their support.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:30.060
On that point, the Food Research Club, which would be disbanded instead of just receiving cuts,

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:33.280
would appear as a reactionary
candidate and quickly gain support.

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:37.420
But if the General Affairs Commission proposed the same policy before us,

00:06:37.420 --> 00:06:39.290
they'd be the ones getting those votes.

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:44.110
The General Affairs Commission would begin their true campaign after the primaries.

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:48.920
They would also release their manifesto to attack Shinonome's weaker stands, too.

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:51.180
And then? How would the votes look?

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:55.480
With the votes from the clubs set for reform and our votes, around 400.

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:56.810
We'd need to make up the rest.

00:06:56.810 --> 00:06:58.280
400?

00:06:59.730 --> 00:07:02.260
Then it's another 200 votes...

00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:04.480
...which is 25 votes from each of us?

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:08.280
We should be able to work something out if we ask our friends.

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:11.360
Non-chan actually knows a lot of people.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:13.070
Non-chan can get us lots of votes.

00:07:13.630 --> 00:07:16.840
And I'm sure some other people will put votes in for us on the day of the election...

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:19.880
...so this might be easy after all.

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:21.710
I don't mind that you're enjoying yourselves,

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:27.720
but I hope you understand that garnering the aforementioned 400 votes is possible

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:28.960
only if you cooperate with us.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:30.660
We understand.

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:33.140
We know that we can't do this on our own.

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:35.700
But what do you mean by "cooperate"?

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:37.260
The Public Safety Commission is on probation, right?

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:41.080
That being the case, we can't
lend you any of our members.

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:46.520
However, we can lend you the know-how regarding the election that we've acquired.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:49.040
The know-how?

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:49.780
Yes.

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:53.040
The know-how of someone who has previously won.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:55.030
Isn't that fascinating?

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:57.660
We should definitely ask for it.

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:02.040
What are you saying? We don't have to ask, right?

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:06.540
Exactly. We are the ones who are asking.

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:10.300
See? We have the high ground here.

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:12.000
We don't need to make any rash promises.

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:15.340
Regardless, you shouldn't be so haughty to someone offering us help.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:16.700
Don't be ignorant, Yuuki.

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:20.100
The president isn't doing this out of the kindness of his heart.

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:25.270
It's possible that he plans on making a puppet government out of you.

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:28.240
That's quite the accusation.

00:08:28.240 --> 00:08:32.570
Nevertheless, I understand that it's
difficult for you to trust me so suddenly.

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:39.720
I would like to propose a limited contract until the primary election ends.

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:45.080
And if you begin to trust us somewhere down the line, we'll extend the contract.

00:08:46.690 --> 00:08:47.750
Deal!

00:08:50.590 --> 00:08:52.340
Thank you very much.

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:54.380
We won't let you down.

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:57.340
Make sure Yuuki wins.

00:08:57.750 --> 00:08:58.850
You can count on me.

00:09:00.270 --> 00:09:00.960
Oojima-kun.

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:02.300
Y-Yes?!

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:04.360
I look forward to working with you.

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:06.600
Same here. I look forward to it.

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:10.230
Yumeshima-kun, let's do our best together.

00:09:10.550 --> 00:09:13.740
Yes, let's... come together.

00:09:19.670 --> 00:09:22.080
Sarue-san, I look forward to working with you.

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:23.230
Yes.

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:25.780
Monzennaka-san, I look forward to working with you.

00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:26.640
Sure.

00:09:31.510 --> 00:09:33.660
Non-chan, let's win this thing.

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:35.010
Let's go win!

00:09:35.690 --> 00:09:36.860
Kiba-san.

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:39.180
Yes.

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:41.860
I look forward to working together.

00:09:41.860 --> 00:09:44.100
Yes, me too.

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:47.100
This is what you call a life-saver.

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:48.350
Don't relax just yet.

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:49.700
Morishita-san... right?
Don't relax just yet.

00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:51.340
Morishita-san... right?

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:52.110
Let's work together.

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:03.330
A mere 400 votes

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:06.420
is much less than what the Public Safety Commission is capable of.

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:09.980
I don't know what you're up to,

00:10:09.980 --> 00:10:14.360
but don't involve my kids in your skirmishes.

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:15.880
I would never.

00:10:16.770 --> 00:10:18.130
Can I believe you?

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:20.140
Of course.

00:10:22.710 --> 00:10:24.280
They're all very good kids.

00:10:24.280 --> 00:10:26.080
Take care of them.

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:28.890
I will do my best.

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:35.620
For starters, we'll save the manifesto for later.

00:10:35.620 --> 00:10:37.280
We're not handling that first?

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:40.660
No one would look at the
manifesto of a bubbly candidate.

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:43.280
How are we going to do this without a manifesto?

00:10:43.690 --> 00:10:47.140
It is not necessary for you to place first in the primaries.

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:49.920
You only need to gather the 600 votes required to pass.

00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:54.800
To do that, you should focus on the most salient policy in your campaign.

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:56.860
"Protecting the clubs," right?

00:10:56.860 --> 00:10:58.040
Precisely.

00:10:58.040 --> 00:11:03.940
So first, Oojima-kun, please visit the clubs faced with budget cuts and ask for their support.

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:05.720
Okay. I'll get right to it.

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:07.440
One moment, please.

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:10.520
In your visit, please bring a female club member.

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:11.740
A female club member?

00:11:11.740 --> 00:11:12.890
Yes.

00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:14.860
There are many clubs with more males than females,

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:19.360
so it'd help to have a female student there to smile and make the request.

00:11:20.430 --> 00:11:21.920
That's a good idea.

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:23.870
He's a pro. A campaigning pro.

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:26.620
So who wants to come with me?

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:30.780
There must be at least a hundred of those clubs, right?

00:11:30.780 --> 00:11:32.880
And I'd have to be stuck with Ooshima the entire time.

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:34.880
You guys...

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:37.900
No one else wants to,

00:11:37.900 --> 00:11:39.520
and I <i>am</i> campaign president.

00:11:39.520 --> 00:11:42.380
I'll do the job if no one else wants to.

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:44.080
There you have it.

00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:47.770
With that out of the way, can someone else handle obtaining signatures?

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:50.770
Signatures... What for?

00:11:51.170 --> 00:11:55.000
People that take the time to sign are less likely to betray us.

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:58.920
They would, to some degree, feel bad about lying.

00:11:58.920 --> 00:12:01.650
Even if it's impossible to determine, they're still likely to vote for us.

00:12:02.010 --> 00:12:04.160
That job sounds just as tedious.

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:05.140
Yeah.

00:12:05.140 --> 00:12:06.410
Hey, guys...

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:08.910
Do you actually feel like helping?!

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:14.160
By the way, this job is most effective when done by pretty girls.

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:15.560
I'm going to get signatures!

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:16.130
Me too!

00:12:19.250 --> 00:12:20.750
Oojima
Yuuki
Election
Headquarters<b></b>

00:12:20.750 --> 00:12:22.090
They're gone.

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:23.320
A pro...

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:25.260
He's pro at making people do as he wants.

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:27.240
I'm just getting started.

00:12:37.370 --> 00:12:39.610
A-An election committee?

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:43.840
Yes. A committee that supports Yuuki from behind.

00:12:43.840 --> 00:12:46.620
It'll consist of clubs targeted by Shinonome.

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:49.040
We'll be fighting against people that have the support of

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:51.620
the Finance Commission and the General Affairs Commission.

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:55.100
However, we don't have that
kind of support for ourselves.

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:57.630
Th-That could pose a problem.

00:12:57.630 --> 00:13:00.340
That's why we need an election committee.

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:03.920
I want you two as the committee's president and vice president.

00:13:04.270 --> 00:13:05.840
President and...

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:07.930
...vice president?

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:12.430
Please? You guys are our only hope.

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:16.350
But this basically means that I can't just vote, right?

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:17.840
That's right.

00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:21.650
We need you to go to each club and set up the election committee.

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:24.070
Isn't that your job?

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:28.220
We want it to form as a volunteer organization.

00:13:28.220 --> 00:13:32.200
It shouldn't appear as though the committee were forcibly formed.

00:13:33.270 --> 00:13:34.540
I see.

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:37.000
Still, this is a lot to be responsible for.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:39.210
We're begging you, Ariake, Garage.

00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:43.260
Please! The results of this election would depend on this committee.

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:48.930
I got it! I have a great idea!

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:54.140
This and this is...

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:56.100
That is a very good idea.

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:56.850
Right?

00:13:57.170 --> 00:13:59.960
Chisato, we'll help under one condition.

00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:01.480
Come here for a sec.

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:04.160
Please give us your signature.

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:05.490
Please!

00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:15.620
Let's see...

00:14:16.110 --> 00:14:20.000
Make this part more concise and easier to read.

00:14:26.930 --> 00:14:28.780
How does this look to you?

00:14:41.510 --> 00:14:45.030
You've got balls to actually come here alone.

00:14:45.310 --> 00:14:47.900
I'll show you who the real boss—

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:50.720
I don't have time to deal with your foolishness.

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:52.540
Come on!

00:14:52.540 --> 00:14:56.760
At least say, "I have no interest in being a boss, but I will never forgive—"

00:14:56.760 --> 00:14:57.660
What do you want?

00:14:59.140 --> 00:15:02.040
Can I get my bonus in advance, Ms. Finance Commissioner?

00:15:02.410 --> 00:15:05.420
I'm not responsible for that. Talk to General Affairs.

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:06.840
Don't be so cold.

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:09.880
Even if we have different mothers,
I'm still your beloved sister, aren't I?

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:11.840
If you don't have anything else to say, I'm leaving.

00:15:14.370 --> 00:15:17.100
Are you disbanding the Food Research Club to annoy me?

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:20.660
Of course not. I wouldn't let my private life influence my public duty.

00:15:20.660 --> 00:15:23.110
It's a decision I came to after a thorough examination.

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:25.700
All right, that's a relief.

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:29.520
If it turned out those kids of mine were in trouble because of me, I don't know what I'd do.

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:33.740
Will that be all? I have a meeting with the election committee.

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:35.990
Oh, how you've grown.

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:37.990
That's my sister.

00:15:37.990 --> 00:15:40.140
Your mother must be so proud.

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:42.000
It's not enough.

00:15:43.370 --> 00:15:45.460
I must surpass you.

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:47.920
I must become the student council president that you couldn't!

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:51.090
Oh, really? If you hate me that much,

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:53.090
why not just fire me?

00:15:56.210 --> 00:16:00.230
At this school, teachers are pretty much hired by the students.

00:16:00.570 --> 00:16:03.960
It'd be a simple task for the
Finance Commissioner, wouldn't it?

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:06.820
Didn't you hear me? I won't let my
private life influence my public duty.

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:08.980
So, you wouldn't mind firing me privately?

00:16:11.270 --> 00:16:13.460
Well, do what you want.

00:16:14.010 --> 00:16:15.960
Good luck with the election.

00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:20.260
I'm a teacher, so I'll support you without letting my private life influence me, too.

00:16:32.870 --> 00:16:34.470
Man, I'm exhausted.

00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:39.060
I never thought that talking to strangers could take so much out of you.

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:40.100
You lazy bum.

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:42.640
Then, just for you...

00:16:45.090 --> 00:16:45.840
Huh?

00:16:49.810 --> 00:16:51.120
What is this?!

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:54.030
We're taking a break, right? Get me some coffee.

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:55.820
You're making me go buy it?

00:16:56.210 --> 00:16:58.180
I gave you the money, didn't I?

00:16:58.180 --> 00:17:01.820
You're my property, so no complaining.

00:17:01.820 --> 00:17:05.830
Jeez... Treat me preciously if I'm your property.

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:07.780
You want the usual?

00:17:07.780 --> 00:17:08.660
Yep.

00:17:14.290 --> 00:17:15.590
You <i>are</i> precious.

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:35.440
Hm. I wonder what I should get.

00:17:35.440 --> 00:17:37.160
You're running for president, aren't you?

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:39.700
Oh, Shinonome-san.

00:17:40.230 --> 00:17:43.120
We're rivals now, Powjima-kun.

00:17:44.090 --> 00:17:45.870
What exactly is "Powjima"?

00:17:46.430 --> 00:17:49.720
I thought your name started with "P,"

00:17:49.720 --> 00:17:51.420
but I must have been slightly mistaken.

00:17:51.770 --> 00:17:54.780
It doesn't start with "P," and you're more than just "slightly" mistaken.

00:17:58.970 --> 00:18:01.400
Let's have a fair election.

00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:03.360
Right. I don't plan on losing, though.

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:05.340
You're very confident.

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:07.350
Until next time.

00:18:13.870 --> 00:18:15.700
What are you grinning so hard for?

00:18:15.700 --> 00:18:16.240
Crap.

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:19.640
So this is what was keeping you! What are you doing, playing nice with the enemy?

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:21.220
No, it's not what it looks like!

00:18:21.220 --> 00:18:24.180
You didn't tell me you were friends with the Finance Commissioner!

00:18:24.180 --> 00:18:26.020
Well, there was this thing with her bike...

00:18:26.020 --> 00:18:30.340
Huh? What about it? You haven't told me anything!

00:18:30.340 --> 00:18:33.390
Oh, right. Chisato! Canned coffee!

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:40.430
<b>I'll wait for you~~~
I want to eat nikujaga~~!</b>

00:18:40.430 --> 00:18:42.120
<i>Nikujaga</i>...

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:48.340
Don't try to trick me! Explain yourself!

00:18:48.340 --> 00:18:51.480
What's going on between you two? Tell me! Tell me!

00:18:58.450 --> 00:19:02.580
Onions, carrots, <i>shirataki</i>, kidney beans, garlic...

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:04.860
There should be some pepper left.

00:19:04.860 --> 00:19:07.080
Oh, I forgot to buy some beef.

00:19:08.730 --> 00:19:11.180
Huh? Is that Morishita-san?

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:14.970
Oojima-kun?

00:19:14.970 --> 00:19:16.000
Ayumu-san.

00:19:16.490 --> 00:19:19.980
<i>Shirataki</i>... Are you making curry tonight?

00:19:19.980 --> 00:19:22.010
You don't need <i>shirataki</i> for curry.

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:24.760
I thought you were substituting it for meat.

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:26.560
I wouldn't do that.

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:31.800
I got it! It's stew!

00:19:31.800 --> 00:19:33.660
With <i>shirataki</i> instead of meat!

00:19:33.660 --> 00:19:35.270
I said I wouldn't do that!

00:19:39.850 --> 00:19:41.110
Thanks for coming.

00:19:43.210 --> 00:19:44.940
Time to eat.

00:19:47.010 --> 00:19:50.920
It's so good! I haven't tasted your cooking in two weeks.

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:53.630
Food prepared by other people sure is delicious.

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:57.250
That's something only a person who regularly cooks should say.

00:19:57.250 --> 00:19:59.670
Don't be so petty.

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:06.810
<b>Chisato
Where are you? Are you out?</b>

00:20:08.210 --> 00:20:09.260
Chisato?

00:20:09.260 --> 00:20:09.850
Yeah.

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:12.850
Did she say, "Hey, Yuuki! Where'd you run off to?!"

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:14.720
Something like that.

00:20:14.720 --> 00:20:17.200
It must be hard having a such a jealous girlfriend.

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:19.180
She's not my girlfriend.

00:20:19.710 --> 00:20:21.360
Are you really not dating her?

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:22.990
<b>Tell your mom that I said hi.
I'm really not.</b>

00:20:24.590 --> 00:20:27.140
Then how about dating me?

00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:29.240
Please don't make jokes like that.

00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:33.250
You're a man, and I'm a woman. I don't think it's impossible.

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:36.720
It's impossible as long as you keep up that look

00:20:36.720 --> 00:20:39.250
that gives away how much fun you're having teasing me.

00:20:39.250 --> 00:20:41.140
Huh? Was I making that kind of face?

00:20:41.140 --> 00:20:45.590
Well, you do something like <i>that</i> again, I'd stop coming over.

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:47.180
Yeah, yeah.

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:52.140
But I still don't get why I did something like that.

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:54.000
It's because you were drunk.

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:55.120
I wasn't drunk!

00:20:55.120 --> 00:20:57.240
If I were, I wouldn't remember.

00:20:57.240 --> 00:21:00.840
I still remember how Yuu-kun's lips feel.

00:21:00.840 --> 00:21:02.280
S-Stop that!

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:06.260
Well, I still want Yuu-kun to make me dinner,

00:21:06.260 --> 00:21:07.910
so I'll be careful to not get on your bad side.

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:10.290
I'd be very grateful for that.

00:21:12.770 --> 00:21:16.340
Thanks for the dinner.
The <i>nikujaga</i> was very delicious.

00:21:16.340 --> 00:21:18.040
You're welcome.

00:21:36.090 --> 00:21:38.220
Well, see you later, Yuu-kun.

00:21:38.830 --> 00:21:40.120
Good night.

00:22:18.770 --> 00:22:23.580
In the classroom, looking out the window,
kyoushitsu no madobe de nagameru

00:22:23.580 --> 00:22:27.530
Watching the sky fade softly into twilight,
yasashii yuugure no sora

00:22:27.530 --> 00:22:31.630
I turn around, and there you are again
furimukeba kimi ga egao de

00:22:31.630 --> 00:22:35.710
Looking at me, you smile
kocchi wo miteta

00:22:35.710 --> 00:22:40.050
"Let's go home," you always say,
issho ni kaerou itsumo no

00:22:40.050 --> 00:22:44.220
Going all the places we go every day
toomawari wo shinagara

00:22:44.300 --> 00:22:48.140
Your fingers are just a step away
mada sukoshi todokanai

00:22:48.140 --> 00:22:54.730
But deep inside me, it hurts not holding your hand
yubisaki ga tada setsunakute

00:22:56.390 --> 00:23:01.370
In my heart, I found all these hopes and dreams
ano hi kimi to meguriaeta kara

00:23:01.370 --> 00:23:05.540
Because on that day we happened to meet
takusan no yume wo mitsuketan da

00:23:05.540 --> 00:23:07.770
Even when I wanted to cry,
nakitai toki demo

00:23:07.770 --> 00:23:11.420
You always stayed right there by my side
itsumo soba ni ite kurete

00:23:11.420 --> 00:23:13.950
I want to thank you so much
doumo arigatou

00:23:13.950 --> 00:23:18.220
What I wrote on that page I hid from you
no-to ni kaita himitsu no pe-ji wa

00:23:18.220 --> 00:23:22.090
Were the words that I just couldn't say
zutto iezu ni ita kotoba

00:23:22.090 --> 00:23:27.850
Now they float forever as whispers on the wind
ima kaze no naka zutto sasayaku yo nee

00:23:27.850 --> 00:23:35.730
Listen close, it says, "I love you so much"
kiite kimi ga daisuki da yo

00:23:41.450 --> 00:23:44.060
You know how there are both sweet, sugary snacks

00:23:44.060 --> 00:23:47.020
and salty snacks like crackers, right?

00:23:47.020 --> 00:23:48.600
You can split them into categories like that, yeah.

00:23:48.600 --> 00:23:51.740
But sometimes there are snacks that have both sugar and salt,

00:23:51.740 --> 00:23:56.660
like the salty crackers with sugar on top or candies with salt on them.

00:23:56.660 --> 00:24:00.980
Those are delicious because of how the sweetness and saltiness complement each other.

00:24:01.590 --> 00:24:04.080
Oojima-senpai, you think so too?

00:24:04.080 --> 00:24:06.700
Next time, Episode 4: Funding.

00:24:06.700 --> 00:24:10.020
I also like cookies baked with margarine.
